# Repo-specific privacy patterns for infra-assistant, one extended-regex per line.
# The shared scripts/check_privacy.sh already covers internal host names, real
# IPs, emails and dated prose. These add what is specific to this repo: a bot
# whose config points at real infrastructure and whose prompt files describe an
# environment, so the danger is a real host name, endpoint URL, chat id, or a
# verbatim persona line slipping into an example, a prompt file, or a fixture.
#
# All examples and fixtures must use .invalid / .example hostnames and the
# RFC 5737 documentation IP ranges only.

# Real SSH aliases / host shortnames from the author's environment.
\b(pve-g3|ct-20[0-9]|ct-21[0-9]|nanopi|ai-host|ha-green)\b

# Internal DNS suffixes.
\.lan\b|\.local\b|\.home\b|\.internal\b

# Real endpoint hints — a non-.invalid grafana/netbox/influx/proxmox/ollama URL.
https?://[a-z0-9.-]*\.(?!invalid|example)[a-z]{2,}[:/][^ "']*\b(grafana|netbox|influx|pve|proxmox|adguard|ollama)

# A real-looking Telegram chat id in prose or a prompt file (9+ digit bare int
# that isn't the example 123456789).
\b(?!123456789\b)[1-9][0-9]{8,}\b.*chat|chat.*\b(?!123456789\b)[1-9][0-9]{8,}\b
